  "description": "Test a Rask app the way a person uses it — no browser, no server, no WebSocket. Page.Visit(\"/products/new\") opens a URL through the real router, and page.Type(\"Tea\").Into(\"Name\"), page.Click(\"Save\") and page.Shows(\"Saved\") find fields by their label and buttons by their text. Page.Render(component) renders one component whose Html reflects the current state; page.On(\"#save\").Click() drives one element and Invoke(id) dispatches a handler by its data-rask-on-* id, each returning the re-rendered HTML. Mail.Fake(), Jobs.Fake(), Cache.Fake() and Clock.Fake() stand in for a battery or the clock for one test. Wraps Rask.Core's live-render + handler-dispatch seam. Reference from your test project; Rask.Core comes transitively from your app's Rask.Server / Rask.Wasm.",
